{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "recurrence_thomas_rhs",
    "description": "A 6-level tridiagonal (Thomas) solve as three causal recurrences feeding a right-hand side: forward elimination cp and dp ascending along lev, then back substitution as yrev, an ascending recurrence on the REVERSED axis (yrev[m] = y[7-m]), so the solve is y = A^{-1} x with A tridiagonal (sub-diagonal -1, diagonal 4 + k/2, super-diagonal -1.5), and D(x[i]) = -y[i]. Chains between recurrences (dp reads cp, yrev reads both) are ordinary edges. The anchor is an exact rational solve, so the class is `algebraic`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "compiled_rhs",
      "recurrence",
      "thomas",
      "tridiagonal",
      "reversed-axis",
      "chained"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    }
  },
